  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{3}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=13$ and ${\\int }_{15}^{11}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=21.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{3}^{15}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{15}^{11}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =21 \\\\ 7{\\int }_{15}^{11}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =21 \\\\ -7{\\int }_{11}^{15}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =21 \\\\ {\\int }_{11}^{15}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{15}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{11}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{11}^{15}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =13+(-3) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
